@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.

   Three localizers by design (design §15 step 3b, Governance's two-marker variant plus
   one): the section owns its Onboarding_* / OnboardingReview_* / OnboardingBanner_*
   keys; SharedResource keeps the genuinely shared vocabulary the widget renders
   (Common_*, Shifts_*, Admin_*) and the three Onboarding_*Label keys MVC's global
   DataAnnotationLocalizerProvider resolves; and the widget's Consents step renders
   Consent's copy through Consent's own _ConsentReviewBody partial. Which of the three a
   given key belongs to is not guessable from the call site — a key looked up against the
   wrong one renders as its own name with a green build and a 200, so
   OnboardingLocalizerBindingTests checks every one of them.

   The review pages use two <vc:> elements, <vc:human> and <vc:access-matrix>, both in
   Humans.Base/ViewComponents/ and bound through the @addTagHelper below. Users' ProfileCard
   is not one of them: it is invoked by name (design §15 step 6). OnboardingPageRenderTests
   covers these, but it lives in Humans.Integration.Tests and self-skips in CI. *@
@using Humans.Base.Extensions
@using Humans.Consent
@using Humans.Consent.Contracts
@using Humans.Base.Enums
@using Humans.Users.Contracts
@using Humans.Onboarding
@using Humans.Onboarding.Controllers
@using Humans.Onboarding.Models
@using Humans.Base
@using Humans.Base.Models
@using Humans.Base.Models.Tables
@using Humans.Base.ViewComponents
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@inject IStringLocalizer<OnboardingResource> Localizer
@inject IStringLocalizer<SharedResource> SharedLocalizer
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Base
